# Every domain the sidecar may reach over the network, and the only list the
# firewall reads. One domain per line; `#` starts a comment.
#
# The image build copies this file to a root-owned, read-only path, and the
# firewall reads only that copy. A change here takes effect when the image is
# next built.
#
# Every entry is egress surface. The firewall allows destination addresses, and
# domains behind shared CDN edges serve many unrelated sites, so each entry is a
# potential exfiltration destination through SNI fronting. An entry also allows
# every subdomain under it, so a specific host is narrower than an apex.
#
# No PHP or Drupal toolchain domains: dependency installs run on the host, so
# packagist.org, repo.packagist.org, drupal.org, git.drupalcode.org and
# api.github.com are absent, and the managed policy denies the mutating
# composer subcommands with a reason rather than a network timeout.
#
# Absent because it is a broad CDN: objects.githubusercontent.com (GitHub
# release-asset downloads).

# Claude Code. claude.ai is an apex because sign-in and the installer use
# several of its subdomains, all run by Anthropic.
api.anthropic.com
claude.ai
# OAuth authorize and callback. A separate registrable domain, so the claude.ai
# apex does not cover it, and sign-in fails without it.
platform.claude.com
# Covered by the claude.ai apex; listed so its addresses are allowed from the
# first resolution, before a lookup has added them.
downloads.claude.ai

# Plugin marketplace clones over anonymous HTTPS; an apex because the clones use
# several of its subdomains, all run by GitHub. No credentials exist in the
# sidecar. Only plugin installs and updates from inside the sidecar use it.
github.com
